.TH start-nqptp 1 "9 October 2025" "HiFiBerry" "HiFiBerry Audio Tools"
.SH NAME
start-nqptp \- Start NQPTP daemon with user validation
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B start-nqptp
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B start-nqptp
script is the startup wrapper for the NQPTP (Network Quality Performance Test Protocol) daemon in HiFiBerry OS.
It performs user validation before starting NQPTP to ensure proper authorization.

NQPTP is a daemon that provides network clock synchronization support for AirPlay 2 functionality.
It must run alongside Shairport Sync to provide precise timing for multi-room audio synchronization.

The script first validates that the current user is authorized to run NQPTP by checking:
.IP \(bu 2
If running as root, start is allowed unconditionally
.IP \(bu 2
If running as a non-root user, the username must match the authorized user specified in /etc/hifiberry.user

If authorization fails, the script exits with code 0 to prevent systemd restart attempts.

After successful authorization, the script starts NQPTP with verbose output enabled.

.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/hifiberry.user
Contains the username authorized to run HiFiBerry services

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, or authorization failure (to prevent systemd restart)
.TP
.B 1
NQPTP startup error

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nqptp (1),
.BR shairport-sync (1),
.BR start-shairport (1)

